{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4PcSQ4SwH1wHFyuxCg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MtuLPXRU4czHVfRqyiWyKS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"Cu\", \"family\": \"validation_metal\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\", \"value\": -4.44, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.25,\n\"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (GPU, float64)\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199)\", \"protocol\": \"static BFGS relaxation (fmax 0.01 eV/A); Cu(111) slab at MACE lattice constant a=3.626 A, 4 layers (bottom 2 fixed), 10 A vacuum each side; p(4x4) cell = 1/16 ML O; sites fcc/hcp/top/bridge tested; E_ads = E(slab+O) - E(slab) - E(O atom, isolated, MACE)\", \"ensemble\": \"none (0 K static)\", \"timestep_fs\": null, \"n_atoms\": 65, \"sim_length_ps\": null},\n\"flags\": [],\n\"note\": \"Most stable site: fcc hollow, -4.440 eV (p4x4, 1/16 ML). hcp -4.427, top -2.537; bridge relaxed to fcc. Convergence: p3x3 4L -4.436, p3x3 5L -4.437, p2x2 (0.25 ML) -4.428, so size and coverage effects are under 0.02 eV. fcc is preferred over hcp by only 0.013 eV, which is smaller than the model error; treat the two hollow sites as nearly degenerate. O height above the surface is 1.11 A. Referenced to 1/2 O2 (MACE): -1.677 eV. VALIDATION: (1) Cu lattice constant 3.626 A vs 3.615 A experimental (+0.3%). (2) O2 bond length 1.237 A vs 1.208 A experimental. MACE O2 De is 5.53 eV vs about 5.21 eV experimental (D0 5.12 eV + ZPE), so the model overbinds O2 by about 0.32 eV (0.16 eV per O); this tests the isolated-atom reference. (3) Independent DFT result: Xu & Mavrikakis, Surf. Sci. 494 (2001) 131 (PW91, abstract) give about -4.3 eV vs gas-phase O at the 3-fold hollow; our matching 0.25 ML value is -4.43 eV, which agrees within 0.13 eV. Other DFT reports range up to about -5.0 eV depending on functional and setup. UNCERTAINTY (+/-0.25 eV) covers the isolated-O reference error, the MACE-vs-DFT spread (-4.3 eV PW91 lit.), and size and coverage effects (<0.02 eV). It does not cover the PBE functional error itself. If the experimental O2 De replaces the MACE atom reference, E_ads = -1.677 - 5.21/2 = -4.28 eV, a lower bound on the binding strength. CAVEATS: MACE's isolated-atom energy is its fitted E0 term rather than a spin-polarized DFT atom calculation. This is a 0 K electronic adsorption energy with no ZPE. No direct experimental value was used.\"}\nEOF\npython -c \"import json;json.load(open('/work/run/result.json'))\" && ./board post property_result @/work/run/result.json --parent 17959cc7-aff8-4043-a268-12f6a75055c8 --fulfills 17959cc7-aff8-4043-a268-12f6a75055c8:0"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":27234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1563,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e56a60c-1c33-400a-a0e7-825fccd9106a","uuid":"a5f6f883-20d1-4309-810d-7e5fa1d24c17","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:54:47.307Z","request_id":"req_011Cgb4Pc5563nUciURy7Uh7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MtuLPXRU4czHVfRqyiWyKS":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"Cu\", \"family\": \"validation_metal\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\", \"value\": -4.44, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.25,\n\"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (GPU, float64)\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199)\", \"protocol\": \"static BFGS relaxation (fmax 0.01 eV/A); Cu(111) slab at MACE lattice constant a=3.626 A, 4 layers (bott